> After the martyrdom of St. Bonif[ace,] Vergili[us] was[ made] Bishop of Salz[burg (]7[66] or 767) and laboured successfully for the upbuilding of his[ diocese as] well[ as] for the spread of the[ Faith in neighbouring] heathen[ countries, especially in] Car[inthia. He died] at Salz[burg, 27] November, 7[89. In] 12[33] he was canon[ized by Gregory IX. His] doctrine that the[ earth] is a sphere was[ derived from] the teaching of ancient geographers, and his belief in the existence of the antipodes was[ probably influenced by] the accounts[ which] the ancient Irish voyagers[ gave] of their journeys[.] This[,] at least[, is] the opinion[ of] Rett[berg ("]Kirchengesch. Deutschlands", II, 236[).]

